# General Notes

Insert may or may not be larger than Read 1 and Read 2 combined.

Exclude contaminated reads when doing a de novo assembly.

If the Q30 of the cycle with the barcode sequence is low, it doesn't matter as much as long as the 
barcode can be identified. 

Undetermined barcodes could be due to index hopping.

Undetermined reads are kept incase in case somebody wants to look at them.

Mis-match tolerance: make sure barcodes have specific distances between them when constructing libraries.

Adapter sequence: at one point in the sequence do is the Illumina adapter read instead of the actual insert.

Trim out adapters first in the pipeline for assembly.

Seqkit can create subsamples that randomly selects reads from within a fastq file, and these files can then be used for Kraken2.

Assembly will be run on each individual sample.

vcf file compares differences between sequenced genome and reference genome.




